WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.246
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book four.

2
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:09.013
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.313 --> 00:00:15.414
Unit twenty-four: E-commerce. Today you will describe market change with the present perfect.

4
00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:18.204
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.887
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.018
E-commerce.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:29.572
E-commerce means buying and selling goods or services online.

8
00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:34.203
E-commerce has grown rapidly in Cambodia since 2020.

9
00:00:34.817 --> 00:00:37.550
Your turn. Say: E-commerce.

10
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.273
E-commerce.

11
00:00:42.017 --> 00:00:43.111
Online store.

12
00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:47.684
Online store means a website or app where products are sold.

13
00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:51.467
Her online store ships handmade bags across Asia.

14
00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:55.188
Your turn. Say: Online store.

15
00:00:58.033 --> 00:00:59.696
Online store.

16
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:01.277
Payment.

17
00:01:02.283 --> 00:01:04.538
Payment means the act or method of paying.

18
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:08.090
QR payment has made online shopping far easier.

19
00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:11.080
Your turn. Say: Payment.

20
00:01:13.933 --> 00:01:14.679
Payment.

21
00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:16.487
Logistics.

22
00:01:17.483 --> 00:01:20.876
Logistics means the organisation of storage and delivery.

23
00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:24.981
Reliable logistics are the backbone of e-commerce.

24
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:28.154
Your turn. Say: Logistics.

25
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.117
Logistics.

26
00:01:32.883 --> 00:01:33.757
Customer.

27
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.980
Customer means a person who buys goods or services.

28
00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:41.036
Every customer receives a tracking number.

29
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.256
Your turn. Say: Customer.

30
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.020
Customer.

31
00:01:48.783 --> 00:01:49.657
Platform.

32
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:54.078
Platform means a digital service that connects buyers and sellers.

33
00:01:54.683 --> 00:01:58.285
Small sellers rely on platforms such as Facebook Marketplace.

34
00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:01.570
Your turn. Say: Platform.

35
00:02:04.433 --> 00:02:05.585
Platform.

36
00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.096
Review.

37
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:11.128
Review means a customer's published opinion of a product.

38
00:02:11.717 --> 00:02:14.204
One honest review persuaded me to buy it.

39
00:02:14.817 --> 00:02:17.179
Your turn. Say: Review.

40
00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:20.918
Review.

41
00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:22.557
Trust.

42
00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.792
Trust means confidence that a seller is honest and reliable.

43
00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:30.370
Cash on delivery helped build trust with new buyers.

44
00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:33.322
Your turn. Say: Trust.

45
00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.017
Trust.

46
00:02:37.833 --> 00:02:41.867
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:42.717 --> 00:02:48.864
Visal, your grandmother has sold fabric at Psar Thmei for forty years. Has online shopping affected her?

48
00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:57.293
Enormously. Her sales have fallen since younger customers started buying on Facebook and TikTok Shop.

49
00:02:58.383 --> 00:03:00.662
Has she tried selling online herself?

50
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:10.254
She has, with my help. We've opened a small online store, and she has already received orders from Battambang and even Paris.

51
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.141
What has been the biggest challenge?

52
00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:23.044
Trust. Customers can't touch the fabric, so we've added detailed videos, and her reviews have helped convince new buyers.

53
00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.631
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:26.483 --> 00:03:29.214
Grammar focus: Present perfect for change.

55
00:03:29.514 --> 00:03:30.701
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:31.417 --> 00:03:33.950
Online shopping has transformed retail.

57
00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:37.709
Her sales have fallen since 2020.

58
00:03:38.617 --> 00:03:42.033
Mobile payments have recently made online shopping easier.

59
00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:55.731
Use the present perfect for changes that began in the past and continue to affect the present, often with since, for, recently, already or so far. With a finished time (in 2019, last year), use the past simple.

60
00:03:56.483 --> 00:04:00.471
Be careful! Don't say: Online shopping has transform retail.

61
00:04:02.433 --> 00:04:05.408
Say: Online shopping has transformed retail.

62
00:04:05.708 --> 00:04:07.719
Has + past participle.

63
00:04:08.533 --> 00:04:11.023
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:13.403
The Market in Your Pocket.

65
00:04:13.703 --> 00:04:21.241
E-commerce has transformed retail across Southeast Asia, where many consumers have skipped computers and gone straight to smartphones.

66
00:04:22.233 --> 00:04:28.703
In Cambodia, the spread of QR payments has made it possible for even small vendors to accept money instantly.

67
00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:35.450
Social media platforms have become marketplaces, blurring the line between entertainment and shopping.

68
00:04:36.433 --> 00:04:43.077
However, trust remains a major barrier, so cash on delivery and customer reviews have played a crucial role.

69
00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:49.967
Traditional markets have not disappeared; instead, many sellers have combined physical stalls with online stores.

70
00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:55.103
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:58.170
Prices blank steadily since last year.

72
00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.880
A, rose. B, have risen. C, have rose.

73
00:05:05.433 --> 00:05:07.526
The answer is B: have risen.

74
00:05:08.683 --> 00:05:12.088
A digital service that connects buyers and sellers is a blank.

75
00:05:12.388 --> 00:05:16.656
A, platform. B, payment. C, review.

76
00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.513
The answer is A: platform.

77
00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.799
Confidence that a seller is honest and reliable is blank.

78
00:05:27.099 --> 00:05:31.321
A, logistics. B, e-commerce. C, trust.

79
00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.994
The answer is C: trust.

80
00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.790
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:50.268
A, E-commerce has grown in 2021.. B, E-commerce grew a lot since 2020.. C, E-commerce has grown a lot since 2020..

82
00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:58.457
The answer is C: E-commerce has grown a lot since 2020..

83
00:05:59.617 --> 00:06:02.545
According to the reading, many traditional sellers have…

84
00:06:02.845 --> 00:06:09.563
A, closed their stalls. B, combined stalls with online stores. C, stopped using QR codes.

85
00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.493
The answer is B: combined stalls with online stores.

86
00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:20.991
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.767
How has online shopping changed traditional markets?

88
00:06:41.583 --> 00:06:43.118
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:43.418 --> 00:07:21.315
Online shopping has changed traditional markets in several important ways. First, many young customers have moved their spending to social media shops, so some market stalls have lost sales. Second, prices have become more transparent, because buyers can compare sellers instantly. However, traditional markets have also adapted: many vendors now accept QR payments and sell on Facebook or TikTok as well. In my view, online shopping has not destroyed markets but has forced them to become more competitive and digital.

90
00:07:21.615 --> 00:07:23.382
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:24.283 --> 00:07:29.292
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect for change.

92
00:07:29.592 --> 00:07:32.779
Today's value is honesty. Always tell the truth.

93
00:07:33.079 --> 00:07:36.114
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

94
00:07:36.414 --> 00:07:39.241
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

